1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E07 -= Weekend.Fantasy =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:01:05,763 --> 00:01:08,332
杰森，晚餐不知怎么办了
Jason, I don't know what we're gonna do about dinner.

3
00:01:08,332 --> 00:01:11,068
要完成报导，我要加班
I've got to work late tonight or I'll never finish that story.

4
00:01:11,068 --> 00:01:13,437
麦克3点钟要看牙医
Don't forget Mike's got that dentist appointment at 3:00.

5
00:01:13,437 --> 00:01:15,840
我可以取消3点钟的病人
I can take him. I cancelled my 3:00 patient...

6
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,373
把幽闭恐惧症推迟到6点
I moved my claustrophobic back to 6:00.

7
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:20,840
那病人懂做饭吗？
Great. Can he cook?

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,220
也许吧，只要不在电梯里就行
Maybe. As long as he's not in an elevator.

9
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,680
算了，我带外卖回来吧
Never mind. I'll pick up something.

10
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:31,100
我们很久没单独相处了
You know how long it's been since you and I have been alone together?

11
00:01:31,460 --> 00:01:32,380
我们现在就单独相处了
We're alone now.

12
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,360
我是说没有孩子打扰.
I'm talking about alone. I mean, without our children...

13
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:37,840
没有工作妨碍，没有衣服间隔
without our work, without our clothes.

14
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,720
妈妈，我的翅膀呢？
Mom, where are my wings?

15
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:52,438
控制中心，看来我要在厨房降落了
Houston, it looks like I'm going to have to bring her down in the kitchen.

16
00:01:52,476 --> 00:01:56,581
妈妈，麦克! 我10分钟后就要排练了!
Mom. Come on, Mike! I've got a dress rehearsal in 10 minutes!

17
00:01:56,581 --> 00:01:59,546
发现敌机，殊死搏斗
Oh, no, enemy plane. Looks like a definite dogfight.

18
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:02,240
-麦克! -妈妈!
- Mike! - Mom!

19
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,860
麦克，别再扫射你妹妹
Okay, Mike, will you stop shooting your sister...

20
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,180
把翅膀还给那小朋友
and give the kid back his wings?

21
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:09,360
好的
Okay.

22
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,880
西弗在中场截到球.
And Seaver steals the ball at mid-court.

23
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:14,900
左边假动作，右边假动作，上前得分!
He fakes left, fakes right, goes up and scores!

24
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:18,900
犯规
Foul.

25
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:22,420
够了，谁最后一个上校车.
That's it. Now the last one on that school bus...

26
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:24,600
谁就要吃一个星期爸爸的煎饼
has to eat your fathers pancakes for a week.

27
00:02:24,809 --> 00:02:26,477
真恶心!
Gross!

28
00:02:27,820 --> 00:02:29,640
-再见 -再见
- Bye. - Later, guys.

29
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:30,220
说得好!
Nice.

30
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,780
对不起，我怎么才能补偿你？
I'm sorry, honey. How can I make it up to you, huh?

31
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,900
这个也许能指引你
Well, see if this gives you any ideas.

32
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,080
“布朗克斯受贿”？
"Bronx gorilla takes bride"?

33
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:43,760
不，这里
No, read that.

34
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,740
“雪山周末度假，189.95元”
"Mount Snow getaway weekend. $189.95."

35
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,920
杰森，瞧
Jason, look.

36
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:55,673
住在哈特里酒店 记得上次我们下榻那里吗？
It's at the Hartley Inn. Remember the last time we we were there?

37
00:02:55,673 --> 00:02:59,207
记得，15年前
Yes. Fifteen years ago.

38
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,580
度蜜月
Right after we we're married.

39
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:04,060
记得我们还没有使用吊车卷呢
As I recall, we never did use our lift tickets.

40
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:06,760
9个月后麦克就出生了
And nine months later we had Mike.

41
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,780
也许当年我们应该去滑雪
Maybe we should have done a little skiing.

42
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,480
找个时间去滑雪也不错
Boy, wouldn't it be fun to do that sometime?

43
00:03:16,827 --> 00:03:19,620
-这个周末怎样？ -什么？
- Well, how about this weekend? - What?

44
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:22,040
对，麦姬，我们就去一把
Yeah, come on, Maggie. Why don't we just go for it?

45
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,880
-真的？ -真的
- Really? - Really.

46
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:29,140
那就好玩了
Boy, it would be so much fun.

47
00:03:29,273 --> 00:03:31,880
算算，189.95乘以2
Lets see, $189.95 times two.

48
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,380
本能不能买半票呢？
Do you think they'd charge full price for Ben?

49
00:03:34,880 --> 00:03:37,380
不!我是说属于我们的周末
No! Because I'm talking about a Ben-less weekend.

50
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:42,120
没有本，没有凯罗，没有麦克
A Ben-less, Carol-less, Mike-less weekend.

51
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,760
你也太挑剔了吧？
That's a pretty exclusive guest list.

52
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,540
我就是个势利鬼
Yeah, well, call me a snob.

53
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,360
我们哪有时间请保姆？
Jason, where are we going to find a sitter on such short notice?

54
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,320
-我有个合适人选 -谁？
- I have the perfect candidate. - Who?

55
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,000
-坐下 -麦克不行
- Sit down. - Not Mike.

56
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:57,480
求你坐下好吗
I beg you to sit down.

57
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:02,440
我们从没让他看家超过6小时
But, Jason, we've never left him in charge for more than six hours.

58
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:05,580
最大的原因是家里有我
Yeah, well, our homeowners policy covered most of that.

59
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,820
拜托，有什么问题？
Come on, what's the problem?

60
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:10,380
他15岁了，却连驾照也没有
Honey, he's 15. He doesn't even have his drivers license.

61
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:13,960
房子不用开走，房子住就好了
He doesn't have to drive the house, he only has to sit in it.

62
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,900
我知道，但这算是个突破
I know, but it's just that it's such a big step.

63
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:21,480
我承认是个突破，我们的突破
I agree. It's a very big step. For us.

64
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,240
什么意思？
What do you mean?

65
00:04:23,894 --> 00:04:28,327
承认孩子长大了也是困难的事
I mean, it's tough to admit sometimes that your kids are growing up.

66
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:32,440
那小子刚把水果投进弟弟头上的光环
Jason, the boy just slam-dunked a grapefruit through his brothers halo.

67
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:37,300
麦克能处理这种情况的
I think Mike should be able to handle something like this.

68
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:41,020
问题是我们能否处理
The question is, can we handle it?

69
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,980
你真的认为可以？
You really think they'd be okay?

70
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:45,600
我真的认为可以
I really think they'd be okay.

71
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:49,600
好吧，若他们能处理 我也能处理
Okay, if they can handle it, I can handle it.

72
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,240
-那就是去了？ -是的
- Then you'll go? - You bet.

73
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:54,580
那就尽情放松好了
And you'll kick back and relax.

74
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,180
杰森，在你面前的是.
Jason, you are looking...

75
00:04:58,180 --> 00:05:01,380
轻松女王
at the first lady of relaxation.

76
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:07,680
好，再说一次紧急电话号码
Okay, one more time. Emergency phone numbers.

77
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:09,920
贴在厨房的冰箱上
In the kitchen, on the refrigerator.

78
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:14,640
好，中毒急救，强酸，强碱，汽油产品
Okay, poison drill. Strong alkalis, acids, petroleum products.

79
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,040
叫救护车，喝牛奶
Call the paramedics and drink milk.

80
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:18,620
还有呢？
Everything else?

81
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,900
去看医生，呕吐
Check with the doctor and throw up.

82
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:24,100
原来是轻松女王
If it isn't the first lady of relaxation.

83
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:28,340
只是确保一下，别小题大做
We're just going over a few things, Jason. Let's not make a big deal out of it.

84
00:05:28,726 --> 00:05:31,691
麦克，给你100块
Mike, heres $100.

85
00:05:32,096 --> 00:05:34,731
不用干活就有100块，谢谢
I was going to do this for nothing, but thanks.

86
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:37,720
紧急情况下才能用
That's for emergency use only.

87
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,300
紧急约会可以吗？
So, like, if we have emergency dates?

88
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,480
说笑啦
Just kidding, Dad.

89
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,480
幽默可以舒缓情绪
I find that humor keeps the little ones at ease.

90
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,820
麦克，谢谢你的提点
Thanks for the tip, Mike.

91
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:50,100
你们要好好相处
Now, we want you guys to all try and get along.

92
00:05:50,314 --> 00:05:54,280
麦克现在做主
Mike is in charge.

93
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:58,000
我保证若出了什么差错.
And I want to reassure you that if anything should go amiss...

94
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,900
必定严明执法
justice will be swift and severe.

95
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,540
爸爸，想出一个权力平衡的机制.
Dad, don't you think there should be like a system...

96
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,320
这样好不好？
of checks and balances here?

97
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:12,000
我同意让麦克掌权.
I mean, I can accept that Mike has a certain authority...

98
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,580
-但我和本需要.. -球棍
- just so Ben and I have-- - Baseball bats.

99
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:18,260
我去开门
I'll get that.

100
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:24,400
下午好，我是百科全书公司的人
Good afternoon. I'm from the Facts Are Us encyclopedia company.

101
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,940
对不起，我的家长现在没空
I'm sorry, sir. But my parents really don't have time at the moment.

102
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,700
他们这个周末要外出
You see, they're about to go away for the weekend.

103
00:06:30,855 --> 00:06:34,184
谢谢，旅途愉快
Okay, thank you anyway. Have a nice trip.

104
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:40,260
麦克，你永远也不应该.
Mike, you should never ever tell someone like that...

105
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:41,600
告诉这种人父母不在家
that your parents aren't going to be home.

106
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:45,860
出师不利
Not off to a great start, Mike.

107
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:51,080
没事，这家伙看上去不像什么连环杀手
Okay. I mean, this guy did not look like the psycho killer type.

108
00:06:51,108 --> 00:06:56,110
这样啊，聪明人，连环杀手是怎样的？
I see. Tell me, smart guy, what exactly does the psycho killer type look like?

109
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:00,060
很好
That's very good.

110
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:01,820
够了，够了
Okay, that's it. That's everything.

111
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:05,960
我们要很晚才能到达酒店
Look, by the time we get to the hotel it might be very late.

112
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,580
-你们今晚要干什么？ -在家玩吧
- What are you guys going to do tonight? - Probably just hang out.

113
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,820
-那么早上打电话给你们 -好
- Okay, so well call you in the morning. - Right.

114
00:07:10,961 --> 00:07:12,891
我们走了
We're out of here.

115
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:17,060
我和爸爸就靠你了，我们深信.
Your father and I are relying on you, Mike, and we have the utmost confidence...

116
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:20,360
你能看管好这房子.
in your ability to take care of the house and...

117
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:20,960
看管好我的孩子
my babies.

118
00:07:25,075 --> 00:07:26,572
滑雪时间到了
Snow time.

119
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:30,440
我们这次是信任你才去的
Now, we wouldn't be doing this if we didn't trust you, Mike.

120
00:07:33,083 --> 00:07:34,718
麦姬，走吧
Maggie, lets go.

121
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:35,880
好的
Okay.

122
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:39,900
再见
Bye, everybody.

123
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:49,960
我做得到
I think I can.

124
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,260
楼梯好像加长了
They've added stairs, you know.

125
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:02,440
-杰森，瞧 -真漂亮
- Jason, look at this. - Looks great.

126
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,280
跟15年前一模一样
It's the same room we had 15 years ago.

127
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:09,200
同样的家具，同样的景色
Same furniture, same view.

128
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:14,060
同样的肥皂，都是一样的
Same bar of soap. Not everything's the same.

129
00:08:14,692 --> 00:08:18,727
不过为了保护我们，厕所清理过
No, they've sanitized the toilet for our protection.

130
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:22,520
酒店当然希望物品耐用
I'm sure they held off as long as they could.

131
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:27,000
记得我们第一晚做些什么吗？
Remember what we did here, that very first night?

132
00:08:27,471 --> 00:08:29,780
你发疯了
You we're crazy.

133
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:32,876
-疯够了吗？ -不知道
- You still that crazy? - Oh, I don't know.

134
00:08:32,876 --> 00:08:36,239
-我挑战你 -加倍
- Come on, I dare you. - Double dare?

135
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,011
成交
You're on.

136
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,100
当年的疯狂还是不减
Still crazy after all these years.

137
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,060
小心
Look out.

138
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:51,640
我们该打电话回家
You know, maybe we should call the kids.

139
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:55,340
谁说我们要打回家？
Did somebody say we should call the kids?

140
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:58,700
-他们似乎很遥远 -是的
- I mean, they feel so far away. - Yeah.

141
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,420
-300英里远 -是的
- You know, 300 miles away. - Yeah.

142
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:07,700
想想看300里外的人会变得多小？
Can you imagine how tiny they'd look from 300 miles away?

143
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:08,740
是啊
Yeah.

144
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:12,640
无依无靠，孤苦伶仃
How lost, how helpless, how abandoned.

145
00:09:13,183 --> 00:09:16,020
麦姬，已经10点过后了
Maggie, it's after 10:00.

146
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,600
明早再打回家吧
We said we'd call them in the morning.

147
00:09:18,222 --> 00:09:20,491
-我明白 -而且本睡了
- I know, but-- - And Bens asleep.

148
00:09:20,491 --> 00:09:23,160
你也不想吵醒他吧？
You really don't want to wake him up now, do you?

149
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:29,040
宝贝，你去解开行李吧
Sweetheart, why don't you just start unpacking or something?

150
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:31,000
好的
Okay. All right.

151
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,680
首先要叠好你的毛衣
I'll start by putting away your sweater.

152
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:41,940
亲爱的，怎么了？
Come on, honey, what's the matter?

153
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:46,080
响了7次，没人接
Jason, the phone's rung seven times, and there's no answer.

154
00:09:47,651 --> 00:09:50,245
8，9.

155
00:09:50,245 --> 00:09:50,420
Eight, nine...

156
00:09:52,289 --> 00:09:52,558
10

157
00:09:52,558 --> 00:09:53,582
ten.

158
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:09,260
杰森，响27次了
Jason, that's 27 rings.

159
00:10:09,973 --> 00:10:12,608
-也许熟睡了 -29次
- Maybe they're sound asleep. - Twenty-nine rings.

160
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:15,540
3个人不会都听不到，30次了
Three people could not sleep through 30 rings.

161
00:10:15,879 --> 00:10:17,979
每次只会响10次
That's only 10 rings apiece.

162
00:10:19,280 --> 00:10:21,980
等等，让我试试
Wait a minute, honey, come on. Let me try. Okay?

163
00:10:22,119 --> 00:10:23,787
也许我打错号码了
Maybe you dialed a wrong number.

164
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:26,020
打错，对，有可能
A wrong number. You're right. I could have done that.

165
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:28,500
虽然没试过，但有可能
I don't think I did that, but I could have done that.

166
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:31,160
怎样？
Well?

167
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:34,900
没人接，暂时而已 才响了4次
No answer, yet. Honey, it's only been four rings.

168
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:37,900
加上我的30次，出问题了
Plus my 30. Jason, something's wrong.

169
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,820
会是什么问题？
What could it be?

170
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,540
烧烤汉堡包
Grilled hamburgers, all right.

171
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:59,440
爸妈会同意我们烧烤吗？
Mike, do you really think Mom and Dad would let us have a barbecue?

172
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:02,680
大惊小怪，我们也不是没试过
What's the big wow, Carol? We've had a barbecue before.

173
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,380
没有在客厅烧烤过
Never in the living room.

174
00:11:05,380 --> 00:11:06,520
她说得有道理
She's got a point there.

175
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,760
好吧，到厨房烧烤
Yeah, all right, I'll do it in the kitchen.

176
00:11:11,835 --> 00:11:14,004
这东西怎么弄？
How's this thing work, anyway?

177
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:15,520
算了，我来
Never mind, I got it.

178
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,400
凯罗，再一个杯子
Carol, hand me another glass.

179
00:11:20,444 --> 00:11:21,941
谢谢
Thanks.

180
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:29,519
麦克，拜托!我不要全熟的!
Come on, Mike, I wanted mine rare!

181
00:11:32,890 --> 00:11:35,559
快!我要救火
Quick, I need something to cover the fire!

182
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:42,060
混帐!要重来了
Unbelievable! Now I have to start all over again.

183
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,160
太迟了，控制不了
It's too late! It's out of control!

184
00:11:50,874 --> 00:11:53,634
今晚看来要出去吃了
Guess this means we're eating out tonight.

185
00:12:06,060 --> 00:12:08,900
麦姬，你的想象力太丰富了
Maggie, I think your imagination has gotten the better of you.

186
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,960
麦克是不会在屋里烧烤的
Mike would not barbecue our house.

187
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,560
发生什么事了？怎么不接电话
Then what's going on? Why won't they answer the phone?

188
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,680
我们冷静想想看
Why don't we just think about this calmly for a minute, okay?

189
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,040
他们不会做傻事
We know they wouldn't do anything crazy.

190
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:22,720
也许是他们一起去玩了
Maybe they just decided to do something together.

191
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,540
好玩的事情
Something they could all enjoy.

192
00:12:28,712 --> 00:12:32,380
“第一章，我爸爸姓菲里”
"Chapter 1. My fathers family name being Pirrip...

193
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:36,860
“我受洗的名字是菲利普，小时候..”
"and my Christian name, Philip, my infant tongue could make of both names...

194
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,480
“我只能把这两个都念成菲”
"nothing longer or more explicit than Pip."

195
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:42,480
我去开门
I'll get it.

196
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:45,580
被你抢先一步了!
Darn, I was just getting into it!

197
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:51,520
记得妈妈的话，别让陌生人进来
Remember what Mom said, "Don't open the door to strangers."

198
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,780
他不是陌生人，我们见过他
He's no stranger. He's somebody we know.

199
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:57,380
-晚上好 -你好，进来吧
- Good evening. - Hi, how are you doing? Come on in.

200
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:00,060
谢谢，只有你们在？
Thank you. Thank you very much. You kiddies all alone?

201
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:04,660
没关系，我能做主
No problem, sir. Any decision that needs to be made, I can handle it.

202
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:08,440
这样的话，我有东西让你们看
In that case, I have something very special I'd like to show you.

203
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:11,021
好了!举起手!
All right! Hands up!

204
00:13:11,021 --> 00:13:13,690
过去沙发那边!
Okay, over by the couch!

205
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:15,100
难以置信!
Unbelievable!

206
00:13:15,459 --> 00:13:18,561
用机关枪就想让我们买你的.
If you think that machine guns gonna make us buy one of your...

207
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:20,280
-狗屁百科全书？ -闭嘴
- stupid encyclopedias-- - Shut up!

208
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,160
拿着
And hold this.

209
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,760
其实，这只是把冲锋枪
Actually, this is a submachine gun.

210
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:33,860
有谁知道发明这种武器的美国人是谁？
Can anyone here tell me who first developed this weapon in America?

211
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:40,420
汤普森，这是一把汤普森冲锋枪
Thompson. This is a Thompson submachine gun.

212
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:43,600
若是有百科全书，你们肯定会知道
Something you might know if you owned a set of my encyclopedias.

213
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:46,280
可是你们的父母就是不买
No, your parents couldn't be bothered.

214
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:50,420
他们都忙于取笑我，你们都在取笑我
They we're too busy laughing at me. You we're all laughing at me.

215
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:54,080
-全世界都在取笑我 -去当喜剧演员就好了
- The whole world laughs at me. - Maybe you could become a comedian.

216
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:59,120
你去当一块猪肉好了!
And maybe you, little boy, could become a pork chop!

217
00:14:05,008 --> 00:14:08,576
-不接电话？ -好主意
- Aren't you going to get the phone? - Good idea.

218
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:21,880
谢谢你的一席话，我现在好多了
Thanks for sharing that with me, Jason. I feel much better now.

219
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,560
打给谁？
Who are you calling?

220
00:14:24,227 --> 00:14:26,930
-打给库斯曼 -好
- I'm calling Ellen Coozman. - Good.

221
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:29,760
喂，艾伦？我是杰森.西弗
Hello, Ellen? Yes, this is Jason Seaver.

222
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:34,040
是的，我们打回家没人接
Yeah, well, we just called the kids, and there was no answer...

223
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:36,140
你们可以到隔壁.
so we just wondered maybe if you could run next door...

224
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:38,240
看一看怎么回事吗？
and take a look at them and....

225
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:41,300
好的，谢谢
Would you? Okay. Good, thank you.

226
00:14:41,311 --> 00:14:43,844
他们回头打过来
She's going to call us right back from the house.

227
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:46,040
我就知道这是错误的
Jason, I knew this was a mistake.

228
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,960
我们不应该丢下他们
We should have never ever left them alone.

229
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:49,540
亲爱的，别慌张
Honey, lets not panic, okay?

230
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:52,200
总会有合理的解释.
I still say there's gonna be some reasonable explanation...

231
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,500
为什么不接电话
why they're not answering the phone.

232
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,160
例如呢？
Yeah? Like?

233
00:14:55,826 --> 00:15:00,725
例如孩子们常常会害怕接电话
Well, like, it's not unusual for kids to become phone-shy.

234
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:04,860
艾伦？对
Ellen? Yes.

235
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,080
什么？不在家？
What? They're not there.

236
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:14,040
天哪，他们去哪里了？
God, where on earth could they be?

237
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,000
不知道
I don't know.

238
00:15:55,218 --> 00:15:57,478
麦克，气色不错!
Yo, Michael, looking good!

239
00:15:57,921 --> 00:15:59,851
你们有身份证吗？
Hey, you kids got IDs?

240
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,600
有，看吧
Yeah, here you go, my man.

241
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:08,600
凯罗.西弗，生于1953年，很好
Carol Seaver, born 1953. Looks good to me.

242
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:11,980
本.西弗，退伍军人，越战兵？
Ben Seaver, army discharge. Nam, huh?

243
00:16:12,703 --> 00:16:14,460
-是的 -战争如何？
- Yep. - How was it?

244
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:15,500
惨不忍睹
It was hell.

245
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:23,780
这地方太棒了
Wow, Mike. This place is awesome!

246
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:26,340
怎么以前不带我们来？
Yeah, how come you didn't bring us here before?

247
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:29,640
你们也知道爸妈多么的保守
Well, you know how old-fashioned Mom and Dad are.

248
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:33,260
没关系了 我明天就逃学来这里工作
It won't matter after tonight because l"m dumping school and starting work here.

249
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,900
-行不行？ -行
- Right, Slash? - All right, Seaver.

250
00:16:36,060 --> 00:16:38,080
保镖越多越好
I can always use another bouncer.

251
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,380
你俩呢？找工作？
What about you two? Looking for work?

252
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:44,500
是的，我要做酒保
Yeah, I want to be a bartender!

253
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:49,040
-我可以做服务员 -可以，宝贝
- I could be a waitress. - You got it, toots.

254
00:16:57,440 --> 00:17:02,080
麦克，你身上有些东西不在我身上
Hey, Mike, parts of me have been missing parts of you.

255
00:17:03,186 --> 00:17:07,391
-把我整个拿去吧 -好吧
- Why not take all of me? - All right.

256
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:11,100
老兄，帮帮忙
Hey, buddy, do me a favor.

257
00:17:11,580 --> 00:17:13,720
-保管一下 -好的
- Keep this for me. - Sure.

258
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,640
-三杯烈酒，一杯调酒 -马上就好
- Three shooters and a bull maker. - Coming up.

259
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,605
宝贝，你去哪里了？
Hey, babe, where you been all my life, huh?

260
00:17:21,605 --> 00:17:23,500
上学了，放开我!
In school. Now, leave me alone!

261
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:25,700
来吻一个，轻轻吻一个，过来
Come here, give me a kiss. Just a little kiss. Come here.

262
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:30,320
小子你给我看好
Hey, watch it, dude!

263
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,780
你有话要说吗？
You got something to say, tough guy?

264
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:38,720
动手啊，正合我意
Go ahead, make my day.

265
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,280
我要报警
I'm calling the Huntington police.

266
00:17:47,030 --> 00:17:47,299
516-555-9622

267
00:17:47,299 --> 00:17:49,733
516-555-9622.

268
00:17:50,867 --> 00:17:53,331
我是个记者兼母亲 这些号码我知道
I'm a mother, I'm a reporter. I know these things.

269
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:58,100
喂，警察局？ 对，我是杰森.西弗
Hello, have I reached the police? Yes, this is Jason Seaver.

270
00:17:59,342 --> 00:18:01,135
对，麦克的爸爸
Yes, Mikes dad.

271
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:05,220
有3名失踪儿童
I want to report three missing children...

272
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,460
失踪至少5分钟了
and it's been at least five minutes.

273
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:12,080
有可能是7分钟
No, it could be seven, it might be seven minutes.

274
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:16,720
我和内子在佛蒙特州 把孩子留在家
My wife and I are in Vermont, and we left the kids alone.

275
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,320
对，让麦克当保姆
Yes, with Mike.

276
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,380
我们打给邻居，邻居过去看 孩子不在家
We phoned the neighbors, and they went to check the house, the kids aren't there.

277
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:25,560
罗宾路15号
15, Robin Lane.

278
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,840
谢谢
Thank you. Yes. Okay.

279
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:30,880
杰森，你没留下这里的号码
Jason, you didn't leave them our phone number here.

280
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:32,860
对，因为我们要回家了
No, that's because we're going home.

281
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,878
开车要5小时
But, honey, it's a five-hour drive.

282
00:18:34,878 --> 00:18:39,260
我们可以坐飞机，再转出租车
We can fly down and well take a cab, okay?

283
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,240
-我们不会在这里 -好的
- That's where we belong. - Okay. Okay.

284
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,080
护目镜拿了没有？
Did you get, you got the goggles, didn't you?

285
00:18:42,819 --> 00:18:44,521
-拿了，谢谢 -好吧
- Please, yes, thanks. - Okay. All right.

286
00:19:13,984 --> 00:19:16,084
见鬼，钥匙折了
I have it, the damn keys bent now.

287
00:19:16,240 --> 00:19:18,460
-没插错钥匙吧？ -这是什么？
- You sure you have the right one? - Well, what does that look like?

288
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:20,660
酒店房间的钥匙
The hotel key.

289
00:19:25,161 --> 00:19:28,490
麦克，怎么了？我很困
Mike, what's going on? I'm tired.

290
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:30,360
瞧，有人进入家里了
Look, there's somebody in the house.

291
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,660
你们跳到车房顶，爬树下来
I want you guys to go down the garage roof, climb out on the oak tree...

292
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:34,620
接着到库斯曼家报警，去
and call the police from the Coozmans. Go on.

293
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:47,851
杰森，他们真的不在家，怎么办？
Oh, no, Jason. They're really not here. What are we gonna do?

294
00:19:47,851 --> 00:19:50,714
打电话到警察局，快
Well check back with the police. Okay, come on.

295
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:58,400
对，对，谢谢
Yes, yes, please. Thank you very much.

296
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,760
警察11点来过，孩子们都在家
Well, the police we're here at 11 :00, and all the kids we're here then.

297
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:03,320
但现在都不在
But, Jason, they're gone now.

298
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,669
我知道，警察局会派人来
I know. They're gonna send another patrol car over right away.

299
00:20:05,669 --> 00:20:07,030
别动!
Freeze!

300
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:10,300
-真快 -举起手，到一边去
- That was quick. - Hands up. Over by the rail.

301
00:20:10,607 --> 00:20:12,200
-不，这个.. -快!
- No, you see-- - Move it!

302
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:12,780
好吧
All right.

303
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:16,940
-我们是西弗家的，我们住在这里 -西弗家的人去佛蒙特州了
- But we're the Seavers. We live here. - The Seavers are in Vermont, lady.

304
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:20,180
不，我们飞回来了，我们就是他们
No, we flew back. We're them. We're home.

305
00:20:20,700 --> 00:20:22,320
好，身份证
All right, lets see some ID, pal.

306
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:26,120
照片照得不好
It's not a good picture.

307
00:20:26,589 --> 00:20:30,225
好吧，你出去把孩子们带进屋
All right, why don't you go outside and get those kids and bring them in here?

308
00:20:30,420 --> 00:20:31,780
-他们在哪里？安全吗？ -找到孩子们了？
- Where are they? Are they safe? - You've found the kids.

309
00:20:32,228 --> 00:20:33,300
他们好好的
Well, they we're fine...

310
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:36,400
后来他们听到鬼鬼祟祟的声音 他们报警了
until they heard some prowlers downstairs and called the cops.

311
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:39,220
不可能是我父母，他们在佛蒙特州
They can't be my parents. My parents are in Vermont.

312
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,800
真是不敢相信
I don't believe this.

313
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:46,140
-孩子们 -且慢
- My babies. - Not so fast.

314
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:48,900
麦克，这是你父母？
Mike, are these your parents?

315
00:20:50,313 --> 00:20:52,948
或者是易容高手
Either that, or somebody's very clever with make-up.

316
00:20:54,851 --> 00:20:57,486
你们去哪里了？真担心你们
Where we're you? We worried about you.

317
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:01,460
谢谢你的玩笑
Hey, thanks for keeping things fun.

318
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:06,940
你们回来干什么？
What are you guys doing here?

319
00:21:07,163 --> 00:21:10,663
晚上叫警察来还不够？
I mean, wasn't it enough to send the cops by once this evening?

320
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,920
我们打电话回家，你们不在
But, Mike, we called and you weren't here.

321
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,820
你们说明早才会打来
You said you weren't going to call till tomorrow.

322
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:18,580
这个不重要，你们去哪里了？
That's not the point, Mike. Where the hell we're you?

323
00:21:18,808 --> 00:21:22,740
莫西太太做了蛋糕，请我们过去吃
Mrs. Moisiodi's made a bundt cake. She invited us over for dessert.

324
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:25,600
接着她放旅游幻灯片
And then she pulled out the vacation slides.

325
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,500
她们去过许多地方
They went everywhere.

326
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:32,820
我们10点打来时，你们去哪了？
But we called at 10:00, Mike. Where we're you then?

327
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:34,280
挪威
Norway.

328
00:21:35,580 --> 00:21:37,300
妈妈，你得记住.
Something to bear in mind, Mom.

329
00:21:37,460 --> 00:21:39,640
全世界的海峡都是一个样的
If you've seen one fjord, you've seen them all.

330
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,620
真的吗？
Is that all true, Carol?

331
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:49,100
其实是点心，不算蛋糕
Well, actually it was more a strudel than a bundt cake.

332
00:21:50,140 --> 00:21:52,809
其余的都是真的
And the rest of it is about right.

333
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:54,920
你们以为我们干什么了？
What did you guys think we we're doing here, anyway?

334
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:11,940
我们发过誓不会把父母的 某些做法.
Remember how we always swore we'd never do certain things to our kids...

335
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:13,280
应用在我们的孩子身上
that our parents did to us?

336
00:22:14,840 --> 00:22:17,640
我们刚刚却用了其中一项
Did we just do one of those things to our kids?

337
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:23,580
难说，我们还算处理得当
I don't know. I think we handled it pretty well under the circumstances.

338
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:26,643
-情况还不算太坏 -还能怎么坏？
- it could have been a lot worse. - How?

339
00:22:26,643 --> 00:22:30,413
有可能是我俩去看莫西太太的幻灯片
It could have been us watching Mrs. Moisiodi's vacation slides.

340
00:22:30,413 --> 00:22:31,876
杰森
Jason.

341
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:37,100
看来我们成为普通的父母了
I guess we turned out to be pretty normal parents after all.

342
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:39,840
麦姬，我们很普通吗？
Oh, no, Maggie. Are we normal?

343
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:43,020
-真可怕 -是啊
- Pretty scary, isn't it? - it is.

344
00:22:45,260 --> 00:22:48,840
普通的父母.
Say, do you think two normal parents...

345
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:50,980
会不会在凌晨3点.
would go out at 3:00 in the morning...

346
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:54,080
出去吃香蕉圣代冰淇淋？
for a double-dipped banana fudge sundae surprise?

347
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:55,300
不大可能
I doubt it.

348
